---
import ContactCta from '../components/ContactCta.astro';
import Experience from '../components/Experience.astro';
import Section from '../components/Section.astro';
import { experience } from '../data/experience';
import { site } from '../data/site';
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const crumbs = [
  { name: 'Home', path: '/' },
  { name: 'About', path: '/about' },
];
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Pontus Burman, founder of Papa Bravo"
  description="Pontus Burman is the founder of Papa Bravo. He has led technology, product and transformation at organisations including Eniro, Unilabs, MedHelp, Trustly, Klarna and Getinge. Stockholm, Sweden."
  path="/about"
  breadcrumbs={crumbs}
>
  <Section narrow>
    <p class="eyebrow">About</p>
    <h1>Pontus Burman</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      Founder of Papa Bravo. The person an organisation brings in when technology, product or a
      transformation needs senior leadership that can also stay close to delivery.
    </p>
    <p>
      Based in Stockholm. More than twenty years across technology leadership, product and delivery,
      in companies with very different constraints — from listed groups to faster-moving product
      companies.
    </p>
  </Section>

  <Section eyebrow="Experience" title="What the career has covered">
    <p>
      The recent work includes product and project leadership at Getinge, CTO at Northfork, interim
      Group CTO at Eniro, Head of Platform at Trustly, IT Director for Northern Europe at Unilabs,
      CIO at MedHelp, and infrastructure leadership at Klarna. Earlier assignments include project
      and line management at Unibet.
    </p>
    <p>
      Before the leadership roles, the foundation was technical: systems, infrastructure and
      consulting from the late 1990s, then project and people leadership. A one-year systems
      engineering education sits at the start of that. Later training includes SAFe Product Owner /
      Product Manager, completed in 2024.
    </p>
    <p>
      The pattern is less a single title than a range: technology and the business, product and
      engineering, interim responsibility and the unglamorous work of making delivery predictable.
    </p>
  </Section>

  <Section eyebrow="Perspective" title="Business, technology, product — and building">
    <p>
      Advice that never meets a backlog, an operating incident or a user tends to stay abstract.
      Pontus still builds and runs digital products, alongside the consulting. That is a practical
      constraint on the leadership work: recommendations have to survive contact with architecture,
      teams, release, analytics and the commercial side of a product.
    </p>
    <p>
      It also means the relevant assignments are wider than a standing CTO or CIO vacancy. They
      include transformation, product direction, how an organisation delivers, technology strategy,
      and turning an AI ambition into something that can actually be operated.
    </p>
  </Section>

  <Section eyebrow="Career" title="Selected career experience">
    <Experience items={experience} detailed />
    <p class="note">
      Roles and years are taken from the previous public Papa Bravo site. Earlier systems and
      consulting work, before Unibet, is not listed organisation by organisation.
    </p>
  </Section>

  <Section eyebrow="Today" title="Papa Bravo">
    <p>
      Papa Bravo AB is the company. The work is consulting and advisory assignments, and the
      products the company builds and operates — My Star Day and Körpasset.
    </p>
    <p>
      Clients work with Pontus. There is no separate layer between the conversation and the person
      doing the work.
    </p>
    <p>
      <a href={site.linkedIn} rel="me noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">
        Pontus Burman on LinkedIn
        <span class="visually-hidden"> (opens in a new tab)</span>
      </a>
    </p>
  </Section>

  <Section id="working-together" eyebrow="Collaborators" title="Interested in working with Papa Bravo?">
    <p>
      Papa Bravo is not running a recruitment process, and there is no open role to apply for.
      There is a standing interest in meeting strong people in technology, product and design —
      for a future role, a consulting collaboration, or building products together.
    </p>
    <p>
      <a href={`mailto:${site.email}?subject=Working%20with%20Papa%20Bravo`}>{site.email}</a>
    </p>
  </Section>

  <ContactCta />
</BaseLayout>
